# .npmignore — excluded from `npm publish` / `pnpm pack` tarballs.
#
# npm/pnpm use this file (falling back to .gitignore only if absent) to
# filter the candidate set defined by `package.json.files`. The `files`
# array acts as an allowlist, so .npmignore can only trim files from
# within the already-allowed paths — it cannot exclude whole directory
# trees that are explicitly listed.
#
# Purpose of this file: keep Python bytecode out of the published tarball.
# Without this, running any .py script locally generates __pycache__ with
# version-specific .pyc files that shouldn't ship to consumers (they're
# cpython-<ver> specific and would be stale for anyone on a different
# Python version).

# Python bytecode — generated by py_compile + runtime imports from
# skills/gateway-api-migration/scripts/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# npm pack leftovers
*.tgz
pack.tgz

# OS / editor clutter that `files` wouldn't normally match but might
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
